      "description": "Watch Rotherham United vs Salford City highlights and goals from League Two on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 12, 2026. Expectations were high as the teams took to the pitch for this League Two clash. Fans were anticipating a closely fought encounter, and the match quickly lived up to the hype with a display of relentless attacking intent. A Breathless First Half On 2026-09-12 , Rotherham United and Salford City engaged in a first-half battle that will live long in the memory. The deadlock was broken early in the 9th minute when Ryan Graydon found the net following a precise assist from Luke Molyneux . The early goal set a frantic pace for the match, but the scoring was only just beginning as both sides pushed forward with numbers. In the 31st minute, Joe Powell doubled the excitement by scoring after being set up by Kallum Cesay . However, the response was instantaneous. Just two minutes later, Brandon Cover pulled one back for his side with a clinical finish assisted by Josh Austerfield . The drama reached another peak in the 35th minute when Rotherham United were awarded a penalty, which Paul Mullin expertly dispatched to keep the scoreboard moving in a chaotic opening period. Red Card Drama and the Final Push The second half maintained the high intensity of the first. In the 55th minute, Ossama Ashley got himself on the scoresheet, though the moment was followed by a yellow card for Abraham Odoh . As managers turned to their benches to introduce fresh legs like Tom Bradshaw and Kelly N'Mai , the match took a decisive turn in the 69th minute. Abraham Odoh received his second yellow card and was sent off, leaving his team to defend their position with ten men. Capitalizing on the numerical advantage, Salford City pressed for an equalizer. Their opportunity arrived in the 74th minute via a penalty. Macaulay Langstaff stepped up and made no mistake from the spot, leveling the scores and setting up a grandstand finish. Despite nine minutes of stoppage time and several late substitutions, including Dan Scarr and Oliver Turton , neither side could find a winning goal in what was a truly captivating contest."
